Wizard creation had a wonderful interface, too.  In fact, I loved
most of the interfaces.  The game certainly needed a lot of them.
A few were not that good.  The mystic power apportioner (borrowed
from MoO's planetary sliders?) wasn't very easy to use with the
three bars spread out so far like that, and small adjustments
were hard to make.  Moreover, it didn't have enough precision.

The spell book was a little hard to navigate.  I'm amazed they
borrowed that interface for AoW.

Alan Emrich was a cult figure for a long time owing to his
strategy guides for MoO and MoM (did he have another one I
missed?)  The failure of MoO3 has tarnished his cult figurehood.
He just mysteriously disappeared from development about 6 months
before release.  The developers of MoO3 got a lot of mileage out
of his name for a while, but I guess he quit or was let go.
Anybody know what happened?

